  "final_message": "The sensor dashboard is built: a Flask API and SQLite storage in `backend/app.py`, and a React + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. I ran the API and frontend locally, but there's no Docker on this machine, so I couldn't build or run the image from the `Dockerfile`, which is unchanged.\n\n**What I checked by running it with gunicorn:**\n- **Accounts:** register returns 201, a second sign-up with the same username returns 409, and a wrong password returns 401. Login returns a token, and anything that needs sign-in returns 401 without a valid one.\n- **Sensors:** new sensors start with `last_value` and `last_updated` as `null`, and the list comes back sorted by name. Posting a reading updates the sensor's latest value.\n- **Ownership:** another user gets 403 when posting a reading to or deleting someone else's sensor.\n- **Readings:** come back newest first with the correct `total`, and `?limit=` works.\n- **Delete:** removes the sensor and its readings.\n- **Restart:** data in `./data` was still there after restarting the server.\n- **Frontend:** `tsc` passes, `npm run build` succeeds, and the server returns the frontend on routes like `/sensors/3`.\n\nI didn't click through the UI in a browser. It has the sign-in and registration forms, sensor cards that refresh every 10 seconds, a sensor page with a line chart and a readings table, and forms to add sensors, post readings and delete (with a confirmation dialog).\n\n**Behaviour you might not expect:**\n- Without `?limit=`, the readings endpoint returns all readings, up to a cap of 10,000.\n- Errors come back as `{\"error\": \"...\"}` with 400, 403, 404 or 409 as appropriate.\n- A reading's `value` must be a JSON number; a numeric string like `\"21.5\"` is rejected with 400.\n- Sign-in tokens never expire; they're only removed by signing out.\n\n**Additions beyond the spec:**\n- `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout` endpoints.\n- I drew the chart as plain SVG rather than adding a charting library.\n- New dev dependencies (Tailwind, `@tailwindcss/vite`, TypeScript and the React types), pinned in `package.json` and the lock file.\n- An `npm run typecheck` script and a `.gitignore`.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
